# Every file under verifications/improved/dim27-triple-partition/ is covered by a SHA-256
# manifest, and all seventeen must verify on every platform:
#
#     cd verifications/improved/dim27-triple-partition && python scripts/verify_manifest.py
#
# (run_all.py runs that too, so a broken manifest fails the suite rather than going
# unnoticed, which is what happened once.)
#
# Line-ending conversion on checkout would change those hashes and make the verification
# unreproducible on Windows. The simplest safe rule is to disable end-of-line conversion for
# everything, everywhere.
* -text

# Binary, so nobody is tempted to diff or convert them
*.npy binary
*.npz binary
*.pdf binary
*.gz binary

# NOTE: this tree contains BOTH line endings -- 166 text files use LF and 51 use CRLF,
# an artefact of two write paths used while the repository was assembled.  No SOURCE OR
# DOCUMENTATION file mixes them within itself.  Both statements are about the ten extensions
# audit.py check 5k opens -- .py .md .txt .cff .json .tex .bib .yml .cfg .out -- and that is
# the scope of the guarantee, written down here on 2026-08-30 because it had not been, and re-measured on 2026-09-07
# after the dimension-25 package was added (the files edited that day were normalised to LF).  One
# file in the tree does mix and is deliberately outside that scope:
# verifications/closed/dim32-44-ers-audit/data/cohn_kissing.html, a downloaded copy of Cohn's
# page.  Normalising an archived artefact would change the thing that was archived, and
# `* -text` preserves its bytes either way.  An earlier revision of this note claimed the mix
# had been normalised; it had not, and the claim was never measured.  audit.py measures it.
#
# NOTHING RESTS ON UNIFORMITY.  `* -text` is what carries the guarantee: git stores and
# checks out exactly the bytes that are here, on every platform, whatever each file uses.
# The dimension-27 package -- the one under the SHA-256 manifest -- is entirely LF, and
# its hashes hold because the bytes are preserved, not because the tree is uniform.
#
# So DO NOT remove `* -text` as redundant.  Without it, 52 files would be rewritten on
# checkout on Windows.  scripts/verify_manifest.py in that package is what would catch it.
